  "id": "2-arachidonoylglycerol",
  "term": "2-arachidonoylglycerol",
  "definition": "2-arachidonoylglycerol (2-AG) is an endogenous endocannabinoid that helps activate cannabinoid receptors, especially CB1 in the central nervous system. Its levels are normally reduced by the enzyme MGLL, and when 2-AG increases, endocannabinoid signaling is strengthened, which can dampen excessive neurotransmitter release and neural activity.",
